{
  "section": "learn",
  "title": "Learn",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-logic-in-programming",
      "title": "What is Logic in Programming?",
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "lb-l1-notes",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "What is Logic in Programming?",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Logic is how a program makes decisions and repeats actions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l1-notes__slide-2",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "There are two main ideas:",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "title": "There are two main ideas:",
              "items": [
                "Decision making -> IF statements",
                "Repetition -> loops"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "startsBlock": false
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l1-notes__slide-3",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Programs use logic to:",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "title": "Programs use logic to:",
              "items": [
                "Decide what to do",
                "Repeat steps",
                "Control the flow of execution"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "startsBlock": false
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l1-example",
          "type": "example",
          "title": "Check if a number is positive",
          "duration": 12,
          "problem": "Input a number and output Positive if it is greater than 0.",
          "code": "DECLARE num : INTEGER\n\nINPUT num\n\nIF num > 0 THEN\n    OUTPUT \"Positive\"\nENDIF",
          "explanation": "The program checks a condition. The OUTPUT statement only runs when the condition num > 0 is true."
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l1-tryit",
          "type": "tryit",
          "title": "Try It",
          "task": "Write pseudocode to input a number and output Even if the number is divisible by 2.",
          "marks": 5,
          "expectedAnswer": "DECLARE num : INTEGER\n\nINPUT num\n\nIF num MOD 2 = 0 THEN\n    OUTPUT \"Even\"\nENDIF",
          "markScheme": [
            {
              "criterion": "DECLARE variable",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "INPUT used",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Correct condition using MOD",
              "marks": 2
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Correct OUTPUT statement",
              "marks": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "if-else-statements",
      "title": "IF...ELSE Statements",
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "lb-l2-notes",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "IF...ELSE Statements",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "An IF...ELSE statement is used when there are two possible outcomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l2-notes__slide-2",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "IF...ELSE Statements: Code pattern",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "pseudocode",
              "text": "IF condition THEN\n    statement\nELSE\n    statement\nENDIF"
            }
          ],
          "startsBlock": false
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l2-notes__slide-3",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "IF...ELSE Statements (3/3)",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Use IF...ELSE when the program must choose between one result or another."
            }
          ],
          "startsBlock": false
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l2-example",
          "type": "example",
          "title": "Pass or Fail",
          "duration": 12,
          "problem": "Input a mark and output Pass if the mark is 50 or more. Otherwise output Fail.",
          "code": "DECLARE mark : INTEGER\n\nINPUT mark\n\nIF mark >= 50 THEN\n    OUTPUT \"Pass\"\nELSE\n    OUTPUT \"Fail\"\nENDIF",
          "explanation": "The program uses IF...ELSE because there are two possible outcomes: Pass or Fail."
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l2-tryit",
          "type": "tryit",
          "title": "Try It",
          "task": "Write pseudocode to input a number and output Positive if the number is greater than or equal to 0, otherwise output Negative.",
          "marks": 6,
          "expectedAnswer": "DECLARE num : INTEGER\n\nINPUT num\n\nIF num >= 0 THEN\n    OUTPUT \"Positive\"\nELSE\n    OUTPUT \"Negative\"\nENDIF",
          "markScheme": [
            {
              "criterion": "DECLARE variable",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "INPUT used",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Correct IF condition",
              "marks": 2
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Correct ELSE branch",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "OUTPUT used for both outcomes",
              "marks": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "loops",
      "title": "Loops",
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "lb-l3-notes",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Loops",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Loops are used when a program needs to repeat actions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l3-notes__slide-2",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Common loop choices:",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "title": "Common loop choices:",
              "items": [
                "FOR loop -> use when the number of repetitions is known",
                "WHILE loop -> use when repetition depends on a condition",
                "REPEAT UNTIL loop -> use when the code must run at least once"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "startsBlock": false
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l3-example",
          "type": "example",
          "title": "Output numbers from 1 to 5",
          "duration": 12,
          "problem": "Output the numbers from 1 to 5.",
          "code": "DECLARE i : INTEGER\n\nFOR i <- 1 TO 5\n    OUTPUT i\nNEXT i",
          "explanation": "A FOR loop is used because the number of repetitions is known."
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l3-tryit",
          "type": "tryit",
          "title": "Try It",
          "task": "Write pseudocode to output numbers from 1 to 10.",
          "marks": 4,
          "expectedAnswer": "DECLARE i : INTEGER\n\nFOR i <- 1 TO 10\n    OUTPUT i\nNEXT i",
          "markScheme": [
            {
              "criterion": "Correct FOR loop structure",
              "marks": 2
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Correct range from 1 to 10",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "OUTPUT inside the loop",
              "marks": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "combining-if-and-loops",
      "title": "Combining IF and Loops",
      "slides": [
        {
          "id": "lb-l4-notes",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Combining IF and Loops",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Most real pseudocode problems combine repetition and decision making."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Use a loop when you need to process many values. Use IF inside the loop when each value must be checked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l4-notes__slide-2",
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Thinking pattern:",
          "duration": 12,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "title": "Thinking pattern:",
              "items": [
                "Multiple values -> loop",
                "Check each value -> IF",
                "Track result -> variable"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "startsBlock": false
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l4-example",
          "type": "example",
          "title": "Count even numbers",
          "duration": 12,
          "problem": "Input 5 numbers and count how many are even.",
          "code": "DECLARE num, count, i : INTEGER\n\ncount <- 0\n\nFOR i <- 1 TO 5\n    INPUT num\n\n    IF num MOD 2 = 0 THEN\n        count <- count + 1\n    ENDIF\nNEXT i\n\nOUTPUT count",
          "explanation": "The loop processes 5 numbers. The IF checks each number. The count variable tracks how many values match the condition."
        },
        {
          "id": "lb-l4-tryit",
          "type": "tryit",
          "title": "Try It",
          "task": "Write pseudocode to input 5 numbers and count how many are greater than 10.",
          "marks": 8,
          "expectedAnswer": "DECLARE num, count, i : INTEGER\n\ncount <- 0\n\nFOR i <- 1 TO 5\n    INPUT num\n\n    IF num > 10 THEN\n        count <- count + 1\n    ENDIF\nNEXT i\n\nOUTPUT count",
          "markScheme": [
            {
              "criterion": "DECLARE variables",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Initialize count",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Loop used correctly",
              "marks": 2
            },
            {
              "criterion": "INPUT inside loop",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Correct IF condition",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "Increment count correctly",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "criterion": "OUTPUT count",
              "marks": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
